Unity USD Toolkit patch to OpenUSD v26.05 (commit 2095fafafd033fa23386d7ec6d58c7cc33974518), applied
after openusd-26.05-lz4-1.10.0.patch: bounds and null checks in the usdDraco and usdAbc file format
plugins.

Applied by Native~/build_openusd.py to a worktree of the pinned commit, never to the clone itself;
its SHA-256 is pinned in Native~/dependency-sources/<platform>.tsv. Every change is marked
"Unity USD Toolkit" in the source. Found by fuzzing the macOS payload (16,000 mutated .abc and .drc
files, each through the importer's full read) and by importing meshes UsdDraco_WriteDraco itself
wrote; every crash site below was hit. Files the plugins write themselves read exactly as before.

usdDraco (pxr/usd/plugin/usdDraco):
1. importAttribute.h: Draco copies byte_stride() bytes per value, a size the file declares; an
   attribute whose stride is not sizeof(T) is now ignored, where it wrote past _values on the heap
   (or past a local T in GetMappedValue). A point's value index is checked against the attribute
   before it is read, and the original point order (PopulateValuesWithOrder) before it is written:
   an order entry outside the values wrote a whole value past the end of _values.
2. importTranslator.cpp, _FindOriginalFaceEdges: walks a polygon with an explicit stack instead of
   recursing once per triangle, and never crosses an edge with no triangle on the other side. A
   boundary edge flagged as added had Face(kInvalidCornerIndex) = 0xFFFFFFFF read and written as
   triangleVisited[] and read as a face; a Suzanne mesh written with polygons preserved hit it.
   Upstream dev still has this code as of 2026-10-17.
3. importTranslator.cpp, _PopulateIndicesFromMesh: every face corner has to name a point and a
   position before the corner table is built (one garbage index made Draco allocate for billions
   of vertices); the corner table is built only for polygon reconstruction, and checked; each
   polygon's edges are followed with find() (operator[] inserted edges) and must form one loop of
   exactly as many corners as edges, within the index arrays.
4. importTranslator.cpp: attribute metadata names its attribute by unique id, which was used as an
   index into the attribute list; it is looked up by id and checked. attributeDescriptor.cpp: an
   attribute found by its metadata must still have metadata when looked up by attribute id.

usdAbc (pxr/usd/plugin/usdAbc):
5. The reader runs Alembic with kQuietNoopPolicy, so a sample Alembic cannot read comes back as a
   null pointer rather than an exception. _CopyGenericValue (alembicReader.cpp) and
   _ConvertPODArray (alembicUtil.cpp) dereferenced it; no sample is now no value.
6. AddOutOfSchemaProperty: a header can say compound for a property that does not open as one; the
   invalid compound was read through a null pointer. Nesting is limited to 256 levels.
7. UsdAbc_AlembicDataReader::HasField/HasValue, where values are read on demand: an exception from
   Alembic or Ogawa is no value (TF_RUNTIME_ERROR) rather than an unwinding OpenUSD.

